@MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress = http://localhost:5039

### Liveness probe
GET {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/healthz

### Readiness probe (database + IGDB reachability)
GET {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/readyz

### Browse games
GET {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/games?offset=0
Accept: application/json

### Search games
GET {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/games?search=elden
Accept: application/json

### Upcoming releases
GET {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/games/upcoming
Accept: application/json

### Active platforms
GET {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/platforms/active
Accept: application/json

### What the signed-in user has recorded about one game
# Entry, playthroughs and review in one read. Needs the Identity cookie.
GET {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/entries/1942
Accept: application/json

### Log a playthrough
# Everything is optional. Leave "type" null while still playing — only typed playthroughs with
# minutes feed the community medians below.
POST {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/entries/1942/playthroughs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "normally",
  "platformId": 6,
  "minutesPlayed": 3120,
  "startedOn": "2026-08-02",
  "finishedOn": "2026-09-01",
  "notes": "Death March, no map markers."
}

### Write or rewrite the review of a game
# A PUT because there is one per game. "playthroughId" is optional and must be one of your own
# playthroughs of this game, or the response is a 400 naming that field.
PUT {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/entries/1942/review
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "The best side quests in the genre. The main story is the least of it.",
  "hasSpoilers": false,
  "visibility": "public",
  "playthroughId": null
}

### Delete the review of a game
# Leaves the entry, the score and the playthroughs alone.
DELETE {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/entries/1942/review

### The signed-in user's tags, with how many games carry each
# Needs the Identity cookie. Tags are the owner's alone: nothing public reads them (ADR 0065).
GET {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/tags
Accept: application/json

### Make a tag
# 201 with a new tag, or 200 with the one you already have under that name in any letter case.
POST {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/tags
Content-Type: application/json
X-MVGL-Request: 1

{
  "name": "Couch co-op"
}

### Put exactly these tags on a game
# The whole set: an empty list takes every tag off. Ids that are not your tags are a 400.
PUT {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/entries/1942/tags
Content-Type: application/json
X-MVGL-Request: 1

{
  "tagIds": [1]
}

### Rename a tag — every game keeps it
PUT {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/tags/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-MVGL-Request: 1

{
  "name": "Co-op"
}

### Delete a tag, taking it off every game
DELETE {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/tags/1
X-MVGL-Request: 1

### How long MVGL members say a game takes
# Public: an aggregate over everybody that names nobody. Always 200 and always three tiers,
# each with the number of playthroughs behind it (ADR 0016).
GET {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/games/1942/community-times
Accept: application/json

### Steam news for the games the signed-in user tracks
# Needs the Identity cookie. Playing and On Hold first, then the wishlist, the backlog, and finished
# and dropped games; up to 20 items, no more than 3 from any one game. Always 200, often empty.
GET {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/user/news
Accept: application/json

### Say who you are on your public profile
# Needs the Identity cookie, and the header every write needs. All three at once; null or blank
# clears one. The avatar is an https address on one of AvatarUrlPolicy.Hosts, stored as given and
# never fetched by the server — see docs/decisions/0056-*.
PUT {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/user/profile
Content-Type: application/json
X-MVGL-Request: 1

{
  "displayName": "Stamen",
  "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4",
  "bio": "Mostly RPGs.\nSlowly."
}

### Export everything the signed-in user has entered
# Needs the Identity cookie. Free and IGDB-free — see docs/decisions/0024-the-ownership-contract.md.
GET {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/user/export
Accept: application/json

### Delete the signed-in user's account
# Irreversible, and it cascades to every user-owned table. The password is the confirmation.
DELETE {{MyVideoGameList.Server_HostAddress}}/api/user
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "your-password-here"
}
